{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:25:08.771Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"63e0ddba1125fddcca9a21e5185c82ad23d695d7e3ffc5dea870ea7655f31344","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's review. I checked the Coastal channels you can see (#coastal-team and #coastal-random) and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Still open per Moss's cheat sheet.\n- Open friction, no ticket number given: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by the warehouse managers.\n- Issue: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. No ticket number given.\n- Request from the 2 Nov 2025 digest: a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. Likely already handled, but I can't confirm that from the notes.\n\n**Needs checking:** The cheat sheet says ticket #4419 is PHL. The 2 Nov digest says Kwame's port account logged #4419 about barge slip 7, which sounds like DMF. Kwame should confirm which account it belongs to.\n\nI left out Ticket #8812 (Door 4B scanner) and the PD-tickets (PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827), because they belong to other accounts. Your Dec 2025 cutover recap, which is a note of yours rather than Moss's, mentions PHL ticket PD-8841 (Gate 4B chassis holds). I didn't include it because it's outside the sources you named, but I can add it if you want."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
